Fenrir’s Sanctuary: The Caged Wolf Domain
Executive Summary: Fenrir’s Sanctuary merges Sukuna’s barrierless Malevolent Shrine with whispering cursed-speech echoes. Canonically, lethal domains guarantee hits and can bypass Infinity
. Malevolent Shrine in particular has no outer shell and “hits anything within its effective range relentlessly”
, only ending if Sukuna is incapacitated
. Cursed Speech forces obedience through spoken commands
. Fenrir’s Sanctuary reflects Wulf’s cold precision and obsession: spectral wolf jaws form a bone cage around the arena, and Wulf’s short commands (e.g. “Hungry!”, “Wolf!”, “Eat!”) echo indefinitely. Each utterance triggers multiple waves of ghostly wolf-fangs. Below we ground this in JJK lore, then detail its name, mechanics (activation, range, barrier status, echo-triggered slashes, timing, energy), three vow-adjusted modes, counters/failures, a sample scene, a comparison table, and visual motifs.

Canonical Mechanics
Domain Expansion: A Domain Expansion is the pinnacle of jujutsu
. Lethal domains embed a guarantee-hit effect, meaning all techniques used inside cannot miss and even bypass Gojo’s Infinity
. Malevolent Shrine exemplifies this: it unleashed Cleave/Dismantle slashes over a vast area
. Only Sukuna and Kenjaku can use such domains without a barrier shell
, making them immune to normal disruption – the shrine “cannot be destroyed by any normal means” and ends only if Sukuna is grievously injured
.

Cursed Speech: Cursed Speech is an inherited technique that wraps cursed energy around spoken words, compelling listeners to obey
. For example, commands like “Don’t move” can paralyze or blast enemies
. Its potency depends on the phrase and user’s skill
. While no official Domain uses Cursed Speech, fan discussions envision domains where every word echoes commandingly. One fan concept has echoing commands like “freeze” locking enemies until the echoes fade
; another suggests repeated commands could keep an effect active until a foe dies
. These ideas guide how Wulf’s domain will handle echoing words.

Domain Name and Lore
Fenrir’s Sanctuary – The Caged Wolf Domain. When Wulf activates it, the air chills and spectral iron bars arch overhead. These bars and skeletal wolf heads form an ethereal cage around the battlefield. Runes glow on the cage as Wulf utters a terse command (e.g. “Wolf!”). His voice carries a strange weight: each word ignites vicious echoes, reflecting his control over sound and fury. The domain embodies Wulf’s persona: deadly calm, single-minded in his obsession. Inside, ghost-wolves prowl the cage, their fangs ready to rend anything that moves. Though the domain surrounds him, Wulf remains still and aloof – the apex predator. The connection to Leora is woven subtly: distant echoes occasionally take on her voice, the only warmth in the storm.

Detailed Mechanics
Activation: Wulf expands Fenrir’s Sanctuary with a swift hand sign and a single cursed word (no long incantation). We assume a baseline radius of 100 meters (example) that he can adjust by vow. The domain instantly manifests an open barrier (no shell)
, so its edges remain undefined.

Barrier Status: The domain is barrierless like Malevolent Shrine
. This makes Fenrir’s Sanctuary nearly indestructible by conventional means: only severely wounding Wulf (to the point he can’t maintain the domain) will collapse it
.

Range: By default ~100m (example). Wulf can, as a binding vow, either expand it (up to ~200m like Sukuna
) or shrink it for added power. In Extended Howl Mode (see below) he might double it. Outside the domain, normal combat resumes.

Echo-Triggered Slashes: Special Ability: When Wulf speaks a command word (e.g. “Wolf!”, “Hungry!”, “Eat!”), that word not only takes effect but echoes repeatedly (initial + 2 echoes, for example). Each iteration of the echo immediately summons a full wave of spectral wolf-fangs that slash across the domain. Timing: The original utterance triggers the first wave; 1 second later the echo triggers a second wave; another second a third wave. Thus one word generates three back-to-back slash waves. Multiple words can stack echoes – up to, say, 3 echoes per word, and at most ~9 total echo-waves active (example limits). Each wave is a full “sure-hit” attack: like Sukuna’s cleave, it will strike any target in range.

Guaranteed-Hit Logic: By default, every wave of attacks is guaranteed to hit anything inside the domain
. The echo effect itself (the command) also is effectively unavoidable – unaware enemies are forced by cursed energy to obey or succumb
. In Echo Amplification Mode (see below) Wulf may sacrifice some sure-hit to magnify echoes, in which case highly skilled opponents could dodge the attacks or silence the echoes.

Interaction with Infinity/Other Domains: Fenrir’s Sanctuary is lethal and barrierless. Its spectral fangs bypass Infinity
 just like Malevolent Shrine. The echoed commands, however, can be countered: a foe focusing cursed energy on their ears can negate Wulf’s words
, leaving only the fang-waves to defend against. In a domain clash (two overlapping domains), Fenrir’s Sanctuary behaves like Sukuna’s Shrine: if its effective area envelops another’s weaker shell, it will break through
. Conversely, if Wulf has removed guaranteed-hit (via a vow), an enemy’s barrier could absorb the waves, as Sukuna showed between their Ultimate domains
.

Energy Cost: Activating Fenrir’s Sanctuary and emitting echo-command waves demands immense cursed energy. Think of 1 minute of domain upkeep plus 3 waves of slashes per word as costing ~100 units (example scale). Stronger words (like “Destroy!”) cost more and cause more backlash
. Overuse risks Wulf’s throat, forcing him to pause or collapse the domain, similar to Cursed Speech’s known strain
.

